# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins. `make build` writes the two commands to
# bin/; `go build ./cmd/hookway` (one package at a time) writes to the repo
# root.
/hookway
/hookway-replay
/hookway-wasm
/bin/hookway
/bin/hookway-replay
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts. These are anchored to the
# repo root on purpose: an unanchored *.out would silently swallow Go golden
# files under any testdata/ directory.
/coverage.out
/replay-store-coverage.out
/coverage.txt
/*.out
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
!**/testdata/**

# Downloaded CI/tooling binaries (promtool, etc.)
.tools/

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Env files. This project is configured almost entirely through environment
# variables (see the validate-examples target), so a stray .env.local holding
# real webhook secrets is the most plausible accidental commit here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Keys and certificates. JWT verification and file-backed secret refs make
# locally generated test keypairs a realistic hazard.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
# Private product planning documents kept at the repository root.
/PRODUCT.md
/DESIGN.md
/VISION.md
/MONETIZATION.md
docs/superpowers/
docs/scratch/
/docs/local-plans/
/docs/plans/hardening/
/examples/production-local/.local*/
*.log
!**/testdata/**
.superpowers/brainstorm/

# Per-machine agent instructions and settings stay out of this repository.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.codex-doc-bridge/
.cursor/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.cursorrules

# Impeccable is local design-tool state, not project source.
.impeccable/
**/.impeccable/

# Generated config-UI WASM/build assets (produced by `make wasm` / `make ui`)
internal/editor/assets/*
!internal/editor/assets/.gitkeep

# Copied into the harness dir by `make wasm-harness`
cmd/hookway-wasm/harness/hookway.wasm
cmd/hookway-wasm/harness/wasm_exec.js

# Frontend (web/) build + deps
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
web/blob-report/
web/public/hookway.wasm
web/public/wasm_exec.js
# tsc -b (composite build) byproducts
web/*.tsbuildinfo
web/vite.config.js
web/vite.config.d.ts

# Generated config-UI bundle for go:embed (produced by `make ui`). The whole
# directory is build output; only .gitkeep is tracked, so the `all:webui` embed
# pattern still compiles on a fresh checkout. With no bundle staged the editor
# serves the tracked internal/editor/placeholder.html instead.
internal/editor/webui/*
!internal/editor/webui/.gitkeep

node_modules/

# macOS finder metadata
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# scratch build output
tmp/
/bin/

# Python build and verification-tool bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

/web/dist-console/

# Documentation publication output is generated inside the web project.
/web/.generated/
.scratch/